# Homesteads: how people came to live out on their own land. came_for says why (fresh_start, faith, land, quiet,
# running, family for children who came with their family, born_here); settler is yes for anyone who came from
# somewhere else. Asked by the player ("What brought you out here?") and talked over between NPCs (the settling topic).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What brought you out here?

== came_here ==
[came_reason] [came_life?]
[came_reason]

== came_reason ==
Just ended up here, I suppose.
Needed a fresh start. Out here, nobody knows who I used to be. {came_for=fresh_start, w=6}
A fresh start. Back home everyone had me figured out already. {came_for=fresh_start, w=4}
Wanted to start over somewhere nobody had an opinion of me yet. {came_for=fresh_start, introvert, w=4}
Fresh start! New land, new me. {came_for=fresh_start, optimist, w=4}
Things went bad back home. This was the only way to make them good again. {came_for=fresh_start, pessimist, w=4}
The Cube God led us here. I believe that. {came_for=faith, w=6}
Faith. We prayed on it, and this is where we were meant to be. {came_for=faith, pious, w=6}
Folks back home didn't care for how we worship. Out here, nobody minds. {came_for=faith, w=4}
I came out with others who believe as I do. It's a simpler life, closer to what matters. {came_for=faith, serious, w=4}
Land. Good soil, and nobody else's name on it. {came_for=land, w=6}
Land of my own. Back home I'd have worked someone else's my whole life. {came_for=land, w=5}
Land, plain and simple. A body's got to own something. {came_for=land, proud, w=4}
Every field here, I cleared myself. Couldn't do that back home. {came_for=land, hardworking, w=5}
Land was cheap. Well, free. Nobody else wanted it. {came_for=land, lighthearted, w=4}
The quiet. Towns are loud, and people are louder. {came_for=quiet, w=6}
Peace and quiet. You hear that? Nothing. That's why. {came_for=quiet, w=5}
I like people fine, in small doses. Out here the doses are very small. {came_for=quiet, introvert, w=5}
Too many people back home, all wanting something. {came_for=quiet, w=4}
Let's just say I needed to be somewhere else for a while. {came_for=running, w=6}
I'd rather not talk about it. {came_for=running, w=4}
Nobody comes looking out here. That's all I'll say. {came_for=running, paranoid, w=5}
I left in a hurry. Didn't stop walking until I got here. {came_for=running, w=3}
I owed some people money. Still do, I suppose. {came_for=running, honest, w=4}
Oh, the land. Definitely just the land. Why do you ask? {came_for=running, liar, w=5}
My folks brought me. Wasn't my choice, but I don't mind it now. {came_for=family, w=6}
Came out with my family when I was younger. Hardly remember anywhere else. {came_for=family, w=4}
My parents wanted land. I wanted to stay. They won. {came_for=family, rude, w=3}
I was born here! This is home. {came_for=born_here, w=6}
Brought me out here? I was born in that house. {came_for=born_here, w=5}
Never been anywhere else. Born right here. {came_for=born_here, introvert, w=4}

== came_life ==
It's hard work, but it's honest work.
Hard going, some winters. {season=winter, w=2}
Wouldn't trade it.                        {optimist}
Some days I wonder if it was worth it.    {pessimist}
Every day's work, out here. Suits me.     {hardworking}
More chores than I signed up for.         {lazy}
It's quieter since [partner] passed. We built this place together. {relationship=widowed, w=6}
We built it all ourselves, the two of us. {relationship=married, w=4}
The children were born out here. They don't know any other life. {listener_type=player, relationship=married, w=2}

# Children have their own way of putting it.
== came_here.child ==
I was born here! It's my house! {came_for=born_here, w=5}
Mama and Papa brought me. It was a long walk. {came_for=family, w=5}
I live here!

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NPCs talking it over (the settling chat topic).

== chat_open_settling ==
[listener]. Ever think about why we ended up out here? [came_reason]
Funny, the things that bring a person out this far. [came_reason]
I was thinking about the old days, before we came out here. {settler=yes, w=2}
Do you ever miss it? Back home? {settler=yes, sentimental, w=3}
[came_reason] [came_life?]

== chat_reply_settling ==
[came_reason]
Same here, more or less.
I don't think about it much. Too busy.    {hardworking}
I miss it sometimes. Then I remember why I left. {settler=yes, w=2}
Never miss it. Not once.                  {settler=yes, proud, w=2}
I was born out here, so I wouldn't know.  {came_for=born_here, w=4}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Chores: greeting someone mid-chore (doing = wood, farming, hunting, fishing, cooking, walking, playing), and remarks
# at the moments that earn them.

== greet ==
[hello] Just getting some wood in.             {doing=wood, w=5}
[hello] Mind the tree, it's coming down soon.  {doing=wood, lighthearted, w=4}
Busy. Wood doesn't chop itself.                {doing=wood, rude, w=4}
[hello] Working the field.                     {doing=farming, w=5}
[hello] Wheat's coming along. Slowly.          {doing=farming, pessimist, w=4}
[hello] Good soil out here. Look at it!        {doing=farming, optimist, w=4}
Shh. You'll scare off the game.                {doing=hunting, w=5}
[hello] Out hunting. Keep your voice down.     {doing=hunting, polite, w=4}
[hello] Fish aren't biting much today.         {doing=fishing, w=5}
[hello] Pull up a rock. Fishing's better with company. {doing=fishing, extrovert, w=4}
Quiet, please. I'm fishing.                    {doing=fishing, introvert, w=4}
[hello] Something's on the fire, if you're hungry. {doing=cooking, generous, w=5}
[hello] Just seeing to the cooking.            {doing=cooking, w=5}
[hello] Out for a walk. Nice day for it.       {doing=walking, weather=clear, w=4}
[hello] Just stretching my legs.               {doing=walking, w=4}

== greet.child ==
I'm helping!                                   {doing=farming, w=5}
I'm fishing! I caught one before! Maybe.       {doing=fishing, w=5}
We're playing!                                 {doing=playing, w=4}

== chore_tree_down ==
Timber!
That's that one.
There she goes.                                {lighthearted}
One more for the pile.                         {hardworking}
My arms are going to fall off.                 {lazy}
Sorry, old tree.                               {animal_lover}

== chore_harvest ==
Good wheat this year.
Look at that. All that from a handful of seeds. {optimist}
Could've been better.                          {pessimist}
Bread for a week, this.                        {glutton, w=3}
Cube God be thanked for the harvest.           {pious, w=3}

== chore_caught_fish ==
Got one!
There we go.
Ha! Supper.                                    {glutton, w=2}
Took its time.                                 {lazy}
A beauty.                                      {proud}

== chore_hunted ==
Got it.
Clean shot. Mostly.
Sorry, friend. We have to eat.                 {forgiving}
That'll feed us for a few days.                {hardworking}
Meat tonight!                                  {glutton, w=3}
